  "$comment": "The narrowing ledger vocabulary, owned by the engine (topos/query/narrowing.py) and published here because the control plane and the front end append to the SAME ledger and cannot import Python from the node. Three repos, one merged list on the response: a member emitted by one of them and unknown to the engine arrives as \"unrecognized\", which is a diagnostic nobody can act on. So a member is added to narrowing.py and to this file first, and only then emitted. Each repo drives a drift test off THIS file. The sets are closed by the mechanism, not by care: on 2026-08-19 _slug(\"Sarah Chen divorce lawyer meeting\") was measured travelling through as_public() fully legible, because all three slug functions were character filters that sanitize without constraining membership.",
